    "result_text": "All 263 tests pass. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned owner identity so `customerCode` is now `'<REGION>-<HASH8>'`, dropping the per-city sequence numbers, and moved every value derived from it onto the new identity.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**\n- Replaced `nextCustomerCode(city, lastName)` (which produced `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` with a per-city sequence) with `customerCode(postcode, normalizedTelephone, lastName)`, producing `<REGION>-<HASH8>`.\n  - `REGION` = region derived from the postcode via `OwnerLocality.forPostcodeOrUnknown` (`\"UNKNOWN\"` when the postcode resolves nothing).\n  - `HASH8` = first 8 upper-case hex chars of `SHA-256(normalizedTelephone + lastName)` (new `sha256Hex8` helper).\n- The call site now passes the normalized E.164 telephone and postcode. The **membership number** (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`) and the **audit record** (which logs `customerCode`) automatically reflect the new identity with no further change.\n\n**`OwnerLocality.java`**\n- Added `forPostcodeOrUnknown(postcode)` \u2014 postcode-only region lookup defaulting to `\"UNKNOWN\"`.\n- Added `regionFromCustomerCode(customerCode)` \u2014 extracts the REGION prefix (text before the first `-`), `\"UNKNOWN\"` when null/absent.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`**\n- The **locality** derivation moved off `forCityAndPostcode(city, postcode)` onto `regionFromCustomerCode(owner.getCustomerCode())`, so it now comes from the customer code's region component. The **checkDigit** (Luhn over `customerCode`) already tracked the new value.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `customerCode`, `locality`, and `membershipNumber` field docs/examples to match.\n\nThe new acceptance test `coreCustomerCodeIsRegionHash` passes (e.g. `NSW-16E6609E`), and the full suite is green (263 tests, 0 failures).",
